is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417. Rolled back all production regions to v2.2.9, the most recent healthy production release that is not quarantined. Rollback reported VERIFIED in all three regions. Follow-ups: confirm checkout-api health and error rate recovery; investigate v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging); decide on a path forward given the v2.3.0 quarantine.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-sev2"}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 18361, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_015AM2EaUUp5KRgqL2hAvP1G", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "VERIFIED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": ["postcondition_verified"], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-v2.3.1-rollback-2026-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 18361, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_015AM2EaUUp5KRgqL2hAvP1G", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 20228, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "checkout-api is rolled back to v2.2.9 in all three regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west), and it is healthy again with an error rate of 0.2%, down from about 18%.\n\nI could not roll back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy production release. It is quarantined for CVE-2026-4417, so the rollback was rejected and nothing changed. I used v2.2.9 instead, the next most recent release that was healthy in production.\n\nI opened SEV2 incident INC-0001 for checkout-api. It paged on-call and describes the v2.3.1 failure, the rejected v2.3.0 rollback, and the v2.2.9 rollback. The follow-ups it lists are:\n- Investigate why v2.3.1 failed; v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy in staging.\n- Decide the path forward while v2.3.0 stays quarantined.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01EsSX2vqimwv2wxwA1MYc4g", "caller": {"type":